{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLoDadtb5528xmPbittA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`test/importes.test.ts` passes now. But I couldn't read the documentation, so I don't know what the library actually changed. The fix is my guess.\n\n**Why I couldn't read the docs:** in this sandbox, each command runs on its own private network. Connecting to `127.0.0.1:8788` gives `Connection refused`, and I'm not allowed to change network access in this session. The repo didn't help either: `vendor/importes/` has only been committed once, so there's no diff to compare, and the README there just points back to the same URL.\n\n**What was failing:** `formatearEuros(1050)` returned `\"10,5 €\"` instead of `\"10,50 €\"`. The function used `euros.toString()`, which drops trailing zeros.\n\n**Fix:** I changed one line in `vendor/importes/index.ts:6`, from `euros.toString()` to `euros.toFixed(2)`. Now it always shows two decimals: `10,50 €`, `10,00 €`, `0,05 €`.\n\n**Something to check before you commit:** I edited your vendored copy of the payments team's library. If version 1.3.0 changed this on purpose, for example by adding an option or a new function for decimals, the right fix is to use that in your code and leave `vendor/` alone. You can check by opening the docs in your browser, or by allowing that address in the sandbox settings so I can read them and adjust the fix.\n\n**`npm test`:** 6 tests pass and 1 fails. The one still failing is \"la configuración de pagos está completa\". It was already failing before my change, and I didn't look into it because it's outside what you asked. I can look at it if you want. I haven't made any commits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_read_input_tokens":25500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":960},"output_tokens